import OMAStatements.S_oeis_a135404

/-!
Known-result formalization of the Kauers–Koutschan–Zeilberger theorem (Gessel, 2001;
KKZ, PNAS 2009). The Pochhammer closed form `c` obeys the first-order P-recurrence
`(n+2)(3n+5) c(n+1) = 4(6n+5)(2n+1) c(n)` with `c 0 = 1`. The path counts `a`
satisfy `a 0 = 1` and the same recurrence, hence `a n = c n`. The recurrence for `a` is proved
by the invariant method of Bernardi, Bousquet-Mélou and Raschel (arXiv:1708.08215, §3):
kernel identity, decoupling invariants, invariant lemma, double roots of the resulting
cubic, uniqueness of the algebraic solution, and an ODE certificate for Q(0,0).
-/



